From 91b7181a5dee077b6366e8e2df87202ccf67c1ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maciej=20=C5=BBenczykowski?= <maze@google.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2020 14:26:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] bpf: Restore behaviour of CAP_SYS_ADMIN allowing the
 loading of networking bpf programs

Restore the CAP_SYS_ADMIN fallback for networking program loads. Android
bpfloader uses SYS_ADMIN without NET_ADMIN; keep its existing access
while also allowing the BPF plus NET_ADMIN capability combination.

Upstream commit: b338cb921e6739ff59ce32f43342779fe5ffa732
Backport notes: apply the fallback to the program types present in the
Exynos 8890 tree. Adapted by ivanmeler.

Signed-off-by: ivanmeler <i_ivan@windowslive.com>
---
 kernel/bpf/syscall.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/syscall.c b/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
index 7d1178772def..c8dab72bc0d5 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
@@ -1198,8 +1198,9 @@ static int bpf_prog_load(union bpf_attr *attr)
 	    !bpf_capable())
 		return -EPERM;
 
+	/* Preserve SYS_ADMIN-only loaders, including Android bpfloader. */
 	if (is_net_admin_prog_type(type) &&
-	    !capable(CAP_NET_ADMIN))
+	    !capable(CAP_NET_ADMIN) && !capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN))
 		return -EPERM;
 	if (is_perfmon_prog_type(type) && !perfmon_capable())
 		return -EPERM;
